description:
MIP-3 sections 4-7 and 11. `crates/muster-vt` today is a text-only headless terminal (write, resize, a per-cell `viewport`, cursor) plus the `KeyEncoder` the seam uses. The daemon needs one libghostty-vt terminal per pane, owned by that pane's threads, and every piece below is already in the pinned headers; the gap is bindings.

Needed:
- `Send` for `Terminal`, justified the way `KeyEncoder` justifies it (`key_encoder.rs:57-60`);
- the formatter, VT and plain text (the replay in a_2XJ1ffNcD and `muster pane read` both use it), and a plain-text screen read that does not cost three FFI calls per cell - agent detection reads the bottom of every pane every few hundred ms;
- reads of modes, kitty keyboard flags, mouse tracking, active screen, scrollback rows, palette and default palette;
- scrollback limits (`GHOSTTY_TERMINAL_OPT_SCROLLBACK_MAX_BYTES`);
- the write-back callback (`GHOSTTY_TERMINAL_OPT_WRITE_PTY`) for query answers, and the effect callbacks: bell, title, pwd, clipboard write, desktop notification, progress. They run synchronously inside `vt_write` and must not block (`terminal.h:75-80`);
- key, mouse and paste encoders configured from a terminal (`ghostty_key_encoder_setopt_from_terminal`, `ghostty_mouse_encoder_setopt_from_terminal`);
- XTGETTCAP / terminfo name, kitty graphics storage limit and media switches (`GHOSTTY_TERMINAL_OPT_KITTY_IMAGE_MEDIUM_*`);
- static linking of libghostty-vt for the daemon binary, while anything in the app process keeps the dylib (a static libghostty-vt collides with GhosttyKit there, `docs/observations/libghostty-9f9b8d1d.md` section 8).

The engine sets DEC mode 2027 at creation today to match herdr; keep that, since detection manifests were written against it.

A fuzz target over the terminal with recorded pane output belongs here or with the daemon: one crash in this parser ends every agent on the machine.
